KG42.register("clusters-84ff6acc675e8195f2b36e9c",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v142-d-K002","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","label":"Electricity and heat products and import/export transaction constraints under coalition conditions","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Electricity and heat products and import/export transaction constraints under coalition conditions","market_meaning":"Coalition membership and operating conditions determine the electricity and heat products supplied by the MG, the feasible import/export directions, and the energy-purchase conditions. The integrated {VIU, Private investor} branch permits export of surplus electricity and does not sell heat to D; the {Private investor, D} branch links electricity and heat supply, required electricity imports, and the residents' self-supply heat option, while retaining the export prohibition and heat-price discount provisions. The electricity and heat products of the grand coalition have been recorded, but the corresponding execution and settlement chains are not yet complete.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["activation","bidding"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Electricity products, heat products, and import/export rights apply separately by the three coalitions; heat supply capability does not mean that any coalition may sell heat, and the capacity constraint that permits export does not cancel another coalition's export prohibition. The regulated price is used for the MG to purchase electricity from the VIU and cannot directly replace the internal electricity-selling price for MG users. bidding retains only the upstream-stage label, and no bidding submission process is inferred from it.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Product definitions and transaction execution jointly answer, under which coalition, what energy can be provided to whom and what energy-purchase conditions are borne, and they have independent transaction meaning. Their physical constraints share references with K001, but transaction permissions and pricing conditions are not merged with the equilibrium algorithm into the same rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Primarily responsible for import/export permission, electricity-purchase and heat-purchase conditions, and the corresponding electricity and heat balances; their quantity and cost interfaces are shared references in K001 and are not counted again as new rules."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Distinguish the electricity and heat product combinations of each coalition and determine the applicable products for the execution provisions; the grand coalition products are retained as a branch still lacking execution support."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e026"],"rationale":"In {VIU, Private investor}, the electricity-only supply scope of the product chain and the no-heat-sales condition of the execution chain complement each other, and both are supported by the model setting in which D does not participate in that coalition; the entire product chain is not treated as a duplicate object of the execution chain."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C010"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g04-E14","v141-b-g04-E16"],"rationale":"In the same {Private investor, D} branch, the electricity and heat product choice is jointly with electricity imports, export prohibition, discounted heat purchase, and heat balance to delimit the transaction scope. The linkage is based on the explicit coalition model and heat-supply choice, and the existence of a product is not interpreted as an unconditional trading obligation."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The avoided-cost export payment and the 20% heat-price discount remain textual clauses and lack complete settlement objects and calculation bases. The source also describes a revenue-sharing electricity-selling price between MG users and the investor, but the existing chain does not represent that construct and it cannot be replaced by P^e; the printed units of the export price and the regulated price also need verification.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-Pe","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g05-e01"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-prop-surplus-allocation","v141-b-g03-prop-cost-of-service-pricing"],"required_work":"Verify the source definitions of the payment basis, metering period, heat-price discount base, and MG internal electricity-selling price, and have upstream supplement a supportable representation of prices and settlement; formulas not provided continue to be retained as gaps."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R004-C007 and C009 transcribe the model statements of no exports, no heat sales, and no need for CHP into zero-variable constraints. In particular, no heat sales and all MG heat output being zero are not equivalent once detached from the model assumptions; the relevant variables are not explicitly listed in some source models.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C007","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C009","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-f_lkt","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-qh_MG_ljt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g04-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the equivalence-transcription premises between variable default and zero constraints, and clarify that they apply only to the original coalition model; retain the frozen expressions and do not upgrade them into a universal obligation for all MGs."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R007 includes the electricity and heat products of the grand coalition, but the execution provisions in R004 mainly cover the other two coalitions. The export prohibition, no heat sales, or all pricing conditions of the two-party coalitions cannot be directly copied to the grand coalition; its complete execution branch is still missing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g04-E21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement the execution and pricing scope based on grand-coalition-specific statements and explicitly inherited constraints, distinguishing inheritable physical constraints from trading rights that require separate support."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G004","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence used in product and transaction assembly all remains unverified and has only candidate-support eligibility for this experiment; the zero-variable transcription, price basis, and coalition scope have not yet been independently source-reviewed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g04-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Humans check the two frozen chains and the coalition-specific transaction interpretations of this cluster; retain the current candidate status and do not regard it as source audit or scientific acceptance."}]},"rule_refs":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R004","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-11593fa2cb05bce9","COMP-9bb045c1ca29e037"]});
